{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","text":"MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"number","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHammerOnPullOff\/number","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV"}],"title":"number","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLHammerOnPullOffV6numberAA14MXLNumberLevelVvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHammerOnPullOff"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlhammeronpulloff\/number"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"title":"MXLNumberLevel","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","abstract":[{"text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHammerOnPullOff":{"title":"MXLHammerOnPullOff","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLHammerOnPullOff","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlhammeronpulloff","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHammerOnPullOff","abstract":[{"text":"The hammer-on and pull-off elements are used in guitar and fretted instrument notation. Since a single slur","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be marked over many notes, the hammer-on and pull-off elements are separate so the individual pair of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"notes can be specified. The element content can be used to specify how the hammer-on or pull-off should be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"notated. An empty element leaves this choice up to the application.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLHammerOnPullOff","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHammerOnPullOff/number":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlhammeronpulloff\/number","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHammerOnPullOff\/number","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV"}],"title":"number","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"}}}